## 4. Recurring bug classes - check every diff for these

Distinct from `FAILURE_PATTERNS.md`, which is the append-only registry of what
already shipped and failed. This is the shorter working list a reviewer scans
**every** diff against, whether or not the class has bitten this repository yet.

**4.1 The sibling sweep.** A diff that adds a guard, validator, escaper or
normalizer almost always leaves siblings behind. Grep the module for every call
site with the same shape and confirm each one uses it. Reviewing only the lines
in the diff is how a fix ships to one of four call sites.

**4.2 The untested test.** A test that passes against the bug proves nothing -
a probe sitting outside the code path, an assertion on a value the change cannot
affect, a mock that answers before the logic runs. Revert the fix, confirm the
test **fails**, restore. If it did not fail, the test is the defect.

**4.3 <BUG_CLASS>.** <Symptom -> what to grep for -> what a clean diff looks
like.>

**4.4 <BUG_CLASS>.** <...>

When one of these actually bites, it graduates: write the incident into
`FAILURE_PATTERNS.md` with its check, and add the matching item to
`SHIP_CHECKLIST.md`, in the same change.

